# oracle (setup only, run 0: the field term of the charge equilibrium at step 0; see the efield note in the report): ReaxFF water cut from examples/reaxff/water (in.water.acks2.field (boundary p p s, efield 0 0 1.0)), tolerance 1e-6 as the example, 10 NVE steps, with fix efield 0 0 1.0 (group all)
# oracle-inputs: w65reaxq_water.data w65reaxq_acks2_ff.water w65reaxq_gauss_exp.txt
# Measured (engine vs native, step 0 pe): loose solve 2.4e-6 relative (-13549.69428 vs -13549.66216); the ACKS2

# press 3.2e-4 relative (-546.75896 vs -546.58131); so this case is compared at rel=1e-3.
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=none rel=1e-3 abs=1e-10
units           real
atom_style      charge
boundary        p p s
read_data       w65reaxq_water.data
pair_style      reaxff NULL safezone 3.0 mincap 150
pair_coeff      * * w65reaxq_acks2_ff.water O H
fix             1 all acks2/reaxff 1 0.0 10.0 1.0e-6 reaxff maxiter 1000
fix             3 all efield 0.0 0.0 1.0
neighbor        0.5 bin
neigh_modify    every 1 delay 0 check yes
velocity        all create 300.0 4928459 rot yes dist gaussian
timestep        0.5
fix             2 all nve
thermo_style    custom step temp pe ebond evdwl ecoul ke etotal press
thermo_modify   format float %.15g
thermo          1
run             0
